# Veda on the real Internet, through QEMU's NAT: nettest's online checks,
# DNS for public names (and a name that does not exist), UDP, TCP to public
# servers, HTTP and ping. The network cards' GUI scripts check them against
# a server of the host's (`nettest local`) and need no Internet; this one
# does, so it is not part of `cargo automation test`:
#
#   cargo automation script verification/real/internet.vts
net ethernet
boot-cmdline "run=nettest"
fail-on "PANIC"
fail-on "nettest: FAIL"
wait-serial "nettest: PASS" 300
